.TH env_get_b 3
.SH NAME
env_get_b \- retrieve an environment variable value with a specified length
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <env.h>

.B const char* env_get_b(const char* \fIs\fP, size_t \fInamelen\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B env_get_b
searches the current process environment (\fIenviron\fP) for an 
environment variable. It compares the first \fInamelen\fP characters 
of the string \fIs\fP against the variable names in the environment.

.SH RETURN VALUE
A pointer to the value part of the environment variable, or NULL 
if no matching variable is found.